Z||000004||Dan010||11-28-2001||08:55 PM||||Where would this test point be?<BR>Also, what would the correct pressure be for<BR>this auto trans. 86 with 90,000||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||11-28-2001||09:09 PM||||The way I adjust the TV cable is to depress the adjustment button and move the cable all the way into the housing (away from the throttle body) - then (by hand) turn the throttle all the way toward the drivers side (full open) and the cable will pull out and adjust itself. Then I pull it out one more tooth and that should be the proper setting. You will know when you drive the car and feel the 3-2 shift point ...... ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dan010||11-28-2001||09:41 PM||||I am starting to understand this adjustment,I think.<BR>Will try it this weekend!!<BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT GT 87||11-28-2001||09:58 PM||||To check upper and lower ball joints ---  Jack up the front and remove wheel , with a jack stand under the outer part of the lower control arm , lower the car so the suspension is now in a normal posistion , All suspension points can now be checked for wear ( except lower a-arm bushings ).Use a pry bar between balljoint and a-arm to check for play . Grab upper a-arm and pull forward and back to check a-arm bushings , (they allways wear out about 100,000 miles )||||reg||1
